window.docContents[0].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhSessionModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhSessionModel":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E › PqxdhSessionModel.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 7 headline theorems depend on it 32 of 130 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nWire-Level send / recv Models and Reachable PQXDH SessionsTrusted in part. Computational/Theorems/ uses ReachablePqxdhSession, firstMessageBody, wirePrekey, and wireWhisper (via SignalSession/PqDir.lean); sendWirePending, sendModelPq, recvModelPq, and honestBundle are checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Defines the CLI's one-byte wire framing (2 ‖ SignalMessage vs 3 ‖ PreKeySignalMessage), the pending-session send model sendWirePending over V1 SPQR (pqxdhSpqrSession), the inductive closure ReachablePqxdhSession of PQXDH-initialized sessions under pqxdhSessionParams, and untagged proof-target helpers (sendModelPq, recvModelPq, honestBundle).\n\n\n\nWire tags\n\ndef wireWhisperL38–39 ↗#WIRE_WHISPER: the tag of a bare SignalMessage on the wire.\n\ndef wirePrekeyL41–42 ↗#WIRE_PREKEY: the tag of a PreKeySignalMessage on the wire.\n\nThe pending-session send model\n\ndef firstMessageBodyL46–54 ↗#The first message's body (message_encrypt, session_cipher.rs:76–115, pending branch): PreKeySignalMessage::new with the session's version, the record's local registration id, the pending pre-key's ids and base key, the pending Kyber pre-key (if any), the session's local identity key, and the encrypted SignalMessage.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 56–66): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.sendWirePending\n\nReachable PQXDH sessions\n\ninductive ReachablePqxdhSessionL70–88 ↗#The sessions a PQXDH handshake starts and send / recv continue, with their identity me and record extras x (constant over the session). Roots: Alice's state after init (initiateState) and Bob's after his pre-key recv (recvPrekeyState), for any model extras, inputs and coins. Steps: the session model's Params.send / Params.receive at pqxdhSessionParams W.\n\n3 declarations not shown (lines 92–128): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.sendModelPq, CryptoVerification.E2E.recvModelPq, CryptoVerification.E2E.honestBundle\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E/PqxdhSessionModel.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhSessionModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhSessionModel"}});